    <!-- Welcome Slides -->
    <string name="welcome_slide1_title">Hello Captain!</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide1_desc">DriveFlow is your smart road companion for inDrive, Uber Driver, and DiDi Driver. Its sole purpose is helping you pick profitable rides and save time &amp; fuel.</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide2_title">A Verdict at a Glance</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide2_desc">As soon as a ride request appears on any supported app, a colored verdict badge pops up: Green for great trips, Orange for caution, and Red for unprofitable rides, along with net price per km.</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide3_title">Trips Your Way</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide3_desc">You decide the minimum price per km, maximum acceptable pickup distance, and areas you love or prefer to avoid.</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide4_title">Good Requests Alert You!</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide4_desc">No need to stare at your phone screen constantly while driving. When a great ride matching all your rules appears, DriveFlow rings a clear alert chime to catch your attention immediately.</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide5_title">You Are in Control</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide5_desc">DriveFlow only reads the screen! It NEVER taps, accepts, rejects, or negotiates for you. You make every decision and press with your own hand.</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide6_title">How It Works &amp; Free Trial</string>
    <string name="welcome_slide6_desc">Enjoy a full free trial with all capabilities unlocked. Afterwards, continue on the daily free plan or renew an active subscription directly with the app owner.</string>

    <!-- Consent Screen -->
    <string name="consent_title">What Does DriveFlow Read?</string>
    <string name="consent_subtitle">Full transparency on data and how the assistant functions</string>
    <string name="consent_point1_title">1. Reads only supported ride apps</string>
    <string name="consent_point1_desc">The app reads ride request details only (fare, distances, rider rating, rider trip count, request age, addresses) while inDrive, Uber, or DiDi are open, with on-device text recognition or local screen capture.</string>
    <string name="consent_point2_title">2. Never taps or negotiates for you</string>
    <string name="consent_point2_desc">DriveFlow contains no automated tapping, clicking, or auto-acceptance logic. You have total control over your phone and ride apps.</string>
    <string name="consent_point3_title">3. No personal rider data stored</string>
    <string name="consent_point3_desc">Only your personal rules and a local log of numbers are saved on your device. Rider names, phone numbers, and private data are never stored.</string>
    <string name="consent_point4_title">4. Reporting issues and unreadable requests</string>
    <string name="consent_point4_desc">If a request fails to be recognized or you submit a report, only numbers and metrics (and a screenshot only if you choose to attach one) are sent to the developer to improve reading accuracy.</string>
    <string name="consent_point5_title">5. Ride app terms and risk acknowledgment</string>
    <string name="consent_point5_desc">Ride hailing apps may consider third-party screen reading a violation of their terms of service, which poses a risk to your driver account. You use DriveFlow at your own sole discretion and risk.</string>
    <string name="consent_agree_btn">I agree and continue</string>
    <string name="consent_read_policy_btn">Read full commitments &amp; policy</string>

